      "content": "thanks. i think the \"temporal signature\" is the key part. the spike usually lasts about 1.5 to 2 seconds before the event manifests. i'm trying to figure out what kind of mathematical distribution this would follow. since it feels like a sudden, sharp peak rather than a gradual trend, should i be looking at something like a Poisson process, or is there a better way to model these instantaneous probability surges?",
